 "text": "Hey, how are you doing? simple and sincere. Start with a friendly welcome, go through names and significant dates, and end with a simple blessing. You can read from a nice card, or each guest can write a little about their life together. It's lovely to have shared memories. A simple ritual can work. Lighting a candle, and saying a few words about love and commitment can do it. Lovely. You could also share a garden cake or a pot of something together, signed by all the guests. That's a nice touch. Great. The simple and sincere ceremony, the story part, and the shared ritual. You've got a lovely wedding without all the formalities.",
